From 4d10feb0213c8f0f6ebb6c652986f3ac292837e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zixuan Zhang <zixuan.zhang.uj@renesas.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:30:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] plat: g3l: add the DISP_RET suspend mode (LowPower Display
 demo)

PLAT_SYSTEM_SUSPEND=disp keeps PD_ISO powered during the system suspend:
the display keeps running, driven by the CM33 firmware from on-chip SRAM,
and the CM33 wakes the CA55 up when the user presses USER_SW3.

BL2: hand the DDR retention CSRs over to the CM33 in SRAM (0x5A000, with
CRC) instead of writing them to the boot media; never resume through BL2.

BL31:
- rz_pwr_domain_suspend(): do not touch RIIC0 (it belongs to the CM33);
  check that the CM33 firmware runs; keep the GIC CPU interface enabled
  and set MHU software interrupt ch4 (SPI 74, CM33 -> CA55 core 0) up as
  the only wake-up source (Group 0, which is also enabled in GICD_CTLR:
  gicv3_distif_init() leaves it off without secure interrupts; Group 1 is
  masked at the CPU interface during the sleep; IRQ/FIQ are routed to EL3
  for the WFI, as in rz_cpu_standby(), so that the interrupt ends it).
- pwrc_disp_suspend(), from SRAM with the MMU off: optionally DDR
  retention entry + PLL4 standby (susp_mode in the shared control block),
  Cortex-A55 Sleep Mode (or plain WFI), WFI until the CM33 reports the
  DDR restored, then continue at the BL31 warm entry point.
- Progress is written to the control block, and optionally to the
  console SCIF (susp_mode DEBUG_UART, works with the DDR in retention).
---
